ype":"Method","_domains":["medical_ai","world_model"],"_tasks":[],"_topics":["neural network in memory","cortex reconstruction"],"venue":"Science","venue_tier":"T1","citation_count":0,"summary_zh":"人工神经网络在内存芯片中重建人类大脑皮层。方法：芯片集成。结果：实时高精度。","summary_en":"An artificial neural network reconstructs the human cortex in a computer memory chip. The method is chip integration. The result is real-time high accuracy.","insights":["芯片集成神经网络","重建人类大脑皮层","实时高精度计算"],"insights_en":["Chip-integrated neural network","Reconstruction of the human cortex","Real-time high-precision computation"],"abstract":"An artificial neural network built into a computer memory chip reconstructs the human cortex with high accuracy in real time"},{"id":"openalex:W7167080056","title":"A sub–10-millisecond neural dynamical system based on phase-change memristors","authors":["Lei Cai","Yaoyu Tao","Chenchen Xie","Longhao Yan","S B Li","Ruihong Shen","Zelun Pan","Xile Wang","Bo Wang","Daijing Shi","Yihang Zhu","Teng Zhang","Yixin Zhu","Xi Li","Zhitang Song","Ru Huang","Yuchao Yang"],"published":"2026-07-02","year":2026,"month":7,"has_code":false,"type":"Method","_domains":["medical_ai","world_model"],"_tasks":["WorldModel","Sim2Real","MedImg"],"_topics":["neural dynamical system","phase-change memristors"],"venue":"Science","venue_tier":"T1","citation_count":0,"summary_zh":"本研究提出基于相变忆阻器的亚毫秒级神经动力学系统。通过精确控制忆阻器导电漂移实现实时计算。实验表明，该系统在表面重建任务中表现优异。","summary_en":"This study proposes a sub–10-millisecond neural dynamical system based on phase-change memristors. Real-time computation is achieved through precise control of the conductance drift of memristors. Experiments show that the system performs excellently in surface reconstruction tasks.","insights":["相变忆阻器实现亚毫秒级计算","精确控制导电漂移提高实时性","表面重建任务中表现优异"],"insights_en":["Phase-change memristors enable sub-millisecond computation","Precise control of conductance drift enhances real-time performance","Excellent performance in surface reconstruction tasks"],"abstract":"High-fidelity geometry for physical-world modeling demands real-time, dense, and differentiable deformation fields on manifolds. Neural dynamical systems (NDSs) using adaptive stepsize integration with embedded neural networks excel at these tasks but still suffer latency on the order of hundreds of milliseconds. In this work, we report a sub–10-millisecond NDS hardware leveraging the precisely controlled conductance drift of phase-change memristors and their multilevel compute-in-memory capabilities. We fabricated a 40-nanometer NDS chip for the challenging surface reconstruction tasks. Compared with state-of-the-art NDS hardware, our NDS design achieves a latency of 2.12 milliseconds (below 10 milliseconds) for single-iteration NDS computations with an error tolerance of 10 −7 and delivers 3.82× to 36.27× faster speed while consuming 11.75× to 24.73× less power. The end-to-end NDS latency through hardware measurements and simulations outperformed graphics processing unit A100 by 50.38× to 478.18×."},{"id":"openalex:W7167011715","title":"The Bipartisan infrastructure law’s impact on drinking water funding for disadvantaged communities","authors":["Samyukta Shrivatsa","Derek Ouyang","Daniel E. Ho","Khalid Osman"],"published":"2026-07-02","year":2026,"month":7,"pdf_url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-026-74287-3","has_code":false,"type":"Method","_domains":["world_model"],"_tasks":[],"venue":"Nature Communications","venue_tier":"T1","citation_count":0},{"id":"openalex:W7167013719","title":"Catalytic Promiscuity and Cascade Reaction Mechanism of Ketosteroid Isomerases for Addition Reactions of Cyclic Enones","authors":["Xuemei Li","Mengsha Li","Yangyang Chen","Weidong Liu","Yiyin Liu","R X Zhang","Chuanfang Wu","Xiang Sheng","鲍锦库","Jinhui Feng","Qiaqing Wu","Dunming Zhu"],"published":"2026-07-02","year":2026,"month":7,"pdf_url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-026-75180-9","has_code":false,"type":"Method","_domains":["world_model"],"_tasks":[],"venue":"Nature Communication